Mixed cache states in installed copies are only partly closed. The buttons ship hidden, the #themer fallback is keyed on html.theme-wired at load, the legacy floating #mnav-btn rule is kept, and mixshell.py tests both directions. Transient cosmetic states remain until the reader accepts the shell update:
- a visible 'Skip to text' link under an old nav.css;
- two theme controls when an old book.js meets a new shell.

The Dropbox build. It has no bar and no pwa.js, and uses index.html as contents with no trials.html. The plan covers it with:
- themecss, nav.css and bar height 0 inlined by make.py;
- the #themer fallback;
- folio arrows read from .chapnav;
- chips as spans, upgraded only off file:;
- up-links to index.html#sec-N;
- 'Find a chapter' built from the page;
- sitecheck --build.
verify.py reflects any of this only after make.py runs, because build/ is gitignored.
